Third-party code
================

Parts of this package are ported from

  camunda-external-task-client-python3
  https://github.com/camunda-community-hub/camunda-external-task-client-python3
  License: Apache-2.0 (copyright the camunda-community-hub contributors)

namely the design of the variable handling, the external task model, the task result semantics
(retries derived from the task's retries) and the fetch-and-lock / complete / failure / BPMN error
request formats, in these files of src/operaton_external_task_client/: variables.py, task.py,
service.py, client.py, aio.py, _api.py, _protocol.py, _outcome.py. The code was rewritten and
modernised (httpx instead of requests, typed API, asyncio support, thread pool worker, Camunda
names and endpoints changed to Operaton's). Each ported file carries a "Ported from" line.
